fuxi: 0128 -- stop the trace from slowing the boot it measures

0126 added a per-layer print gated on fuxi_fb_path_logged <= 6, but that counter stops
advancing at 6 (the increment sits behind a < 6 test), so the condition stayed true and
every present printed twice -- 205 of 242 log lines in 22 s, each one formatting,
writing the console and shipping over USB.  The compositor was spending its time talking
about frames instead of drawing them.

The per-layer print is gone and the path print is bounded on its own counter.  Measured
effect on boot progress should be immediate and large; the boot was at 20% after 165 s
with the storm in place.

Harness: applied=127 skipped=0.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -542,6 +542,7 @@
 			fuxi_fb_path_logged++;
 			IOLog("FUXI FB: present via MDP (direct) swap %u\n", get32(rec, 0x50));
 		}
+		/* Path logging must stay bounded: see 0128. */
 		if (!fConsolePaused) {
 			int quiet = 0;
 			fConsolePaused = true;
@@ -597,10 +598,6 @@
